To draw a chessboard in LaTeX representing a specific FEN (Forsyth-Edwards Notation) state, you can use the `chessboard` package. Here's a basic example of how to do it:

```latex
\documentclass{article}
\usepackage{chessboard}

\begin{document}

\chessboard[
    setup=your_fen_notation_here,
    showmover=false,
    label=false,
    margin=1ex,
    boardfontsize=12pt
]

\end{document}
```

Replace `your_fen_notation_here` with your actual FEN notation. For example, the starting position of a chess game is represented by the FEN notation `rnbqkbnr/pppppppp/8/8/8/8/PPPPPPPP/RNBQKBNR`. 

Make sure to include the `chessboard` package in your LaTeX document's preamble. If you don't have the package installed, you can download it from CTAN (Comprehensive TeX Archive Network) or use your LaTeX distribution's package manager to install it.

